# The worker's Redis user: the key families it reads and writes, and the
# commands it sends (security review 2026-10-15, E2-6). The ONE home of the
# rules: both compose files' Redis loads them (deploy/redis/start.sh), an
# operator with an external Redis creates the user from them (docs/redis-
# worker-user.md), and scripts/tests/redis-worker-acl-test.sh drives every
# family through a real Redis with them.
#
# One rule per line; `#` lines and blank lines are ignored. A worker key
# family added in code without a line here is refused by Redis, and every
# dispatch that needs it fails — add the line in the same change.
#
# Dispatch replay guard (worker/src/dispatch_replay.rs): SET NX PX.
~talos:jobnonce:*
# Job idempotency (talos-worker-runtime job_idempotency): GET, SET EX, DEL.
~talos:idem:*
# Sealed module results (runtime.rs): GET, TTL, SETEX.
~wasm:result:*
# Module bytes the CONTROLLER caches for a `redis:wasm:` URI: read only.
%R~wasm:*
# OCI layer cache (module_fetcher.rs): GET, SET EX, DEL.
~oci_cache:*
# The guest cache interface (host/cache.rs), user-prefixed by the host.
~talos_cache:*
# The tier-2 expose_secret daily cap (host/secrets.rs): EVAL INCR/EXPIRE.
~talos:tier2_expose:*
# Local-LLM fleet admission, shared with the controller (talos-local-inference).
~talos:llm-admit:*
# Approval reply topics (host/governance.rs), read by the controller.
~approval:*
resetchannels
-@all
+get
+set
+setex
+del
+exists
+mget
+expire
+ttl
+multi
+exec
+eval
+evalsha
+script|load
+incr
+incrby
+pexpire
+time
+zadd
+zrem
+zscore
+zcard
+zrank
+zrangebyscore
+zremrangebyscore
+ping
+client|setinfo
+acl|whoami
